<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adel Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1749</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ali Qoli Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adel Shah, born Ali Qoli Khan, was a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> who took part in the conspiracy against him and became shah of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> after Nader's murder in 1747. He had most of Nader's family killed and ordered the castration of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> prince Agha Mohammad Khan. Overthrown by his brother Ebrahim in 1748, he was blinded and executed in 1749.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adel-shah.jpg" alt="Adel Shah" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Adel_Shah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
